            Manhattan Active SCALE Documentation
        Work Profile Authorization Retrieval Exit Point
    
    

                Collapse All
                Expand All
            
        View with Navigation Tools
    
    
Integration Endpoints
 > Exit points
 > Work Profile Authorization Retrieval Exit Point
    
    
    
        The system provides an exit point Work Profile Authorization Retrieval , that should be used to override the list of work profiles that can be viewed in various screens. The sql utility function ModifyCharacterSeparatedStringList can be used to modify work profiles in stored procedure exit point programs.

 

The following example represents a sample implementation of the Work Profile Authorization Retrieval exit point program using a stored procedure. 


    
        
            
                Sample exit point program for Work Profile Authorization Retrieval exit point

                
                    
                        Copy Code
                    
                
            

            
                
                    
CREATE PROCEDURE [EXP_WorkProfileAuthorizationRetrieval] (
    @SESSIONVALUE xml,
    @WORKPROFILELIST nvarchar(max),
    @RETURNVALUE nvarchar(max) output
)
AS
    SET NOCOUNT ON;
    DECLARE @workProfilesToAdd nvarchar(max), @workProfilesToRemove nvarchar(max);
    SET @workProfilesToAdd = '';
    SET @workProfilesToRemove = '';

        -- Update the list using Pipe character as the separator
        SELECT @RETURNVALUE = dbo.ModifyCharacterSeparatedStringList(@WORKPROFILELIST, @workProfilesToAdd, @workProfilesToRemove, '|')
           

                
            
        
    


 

            
        
    
    

